diff --git a/.github/workflows/jellyfin.yml b/.github/workflows/jellyfin.yml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8261fc1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.github/workflows/jellyfin.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+name: Jellyfin checks and iOS build
+
+on:
+  workflow_dispatch:
+    inputs:
+      build_app:
+        description: "Also attempt an unsigned iOS build (large dependency download)"
+        type: boolean
+        default: false
+
+permissions:
+  contents: read
+
+jobs:
+  client-tests:
+    runs-on: macos-15
+    timeout-minutes: 15
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      - name: Run Jellyfin client tests
+        run: swift test
+
+  ios-build:
+    if: ${{ inputs.build_app }}
+    needs: client-tests
+    runs-on: macos-15
+    timeout-minutes: 90
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+        with:
+          lfs: true
+          submodules: recursive
+      - name: Fetch dependency binaries
+        run: git submodule foreach --recursive 'git lfs pull'
+      - name: Install Boost
+        run: brew list boost >/dev/null 2>&1 || brew install boost
+      - name: Archive unsigned iOS app
+        run: |
+          set -o pipefail
+          xcodebuild -project ManicEmu/ManicEmu.xcodeproj \
+            -scheme ManicEmuSideload -configuration SideloadRelease \
+            -destination 'generic/platform=iOS' \
+            -archivePath "$RUNNER_TEMP/ManicEMU.xcarchive" \
+            CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO \
+            archive 2>&1 | tee "$RUNNER_TEMP/xcodebuild.log"
+      - name: Package unsigned IPA
+        run: |
+          mkdir -p "$RUNNER_TEMP/ipa/Payload"
+          cp -R "$RUNNER_TEMP/ManicEMU.xcarchive/Products/Applications/"*.app "$RUNNER_TEMP/ipa/Payload/"
+          cd "$RUNNER_TEMP/ipa"
+          ditto -c -k --sequesterRsrc --keepParent Payload "$RUNNER_TEMP/ManicEMU-Jellyfin-unsigned.ipa"
+      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
+        with:
+          name: ManicEMU-Jellyfin-unsigned
+          path: ${{ runner.temp }}/ManicEMU-Jellyfin-unsigned.ipa
+          if-no-files-found: error
+      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
+        if: always()
+        with:
+          name: iOS-build-log
+          path: ${{ runner.temp }}/xcodebuild.log
+          if-no-files-found: ignore
diff --git a/JELLYFIN.md b/JELLYFIN.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1de63fb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/JELLYFIN.md
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+# Jellyfin game library integration
+
+Source implementation based on Manic-EMU/ManicEMU commit `b1d82af8dbd37ab9995ad44a4334ea90e3c22b6f`.
+
+## Using it
+
+Open **Import Ã¢â€ â€™ Add service Ã¢â€ â€™ Game libraries Ã¢â€ â€™ Jellyfin**. Enter your server's full URL (including a reverse-proxy base path if applicable), username, and password. Select the library containing your games. Open console folders such as NES or Super Nintendo, then select a game. Back moves to the parent folder; Libraries returns to the library list. Search finds games in the current folder and its subfolders. Browse covers, select a game, and keep the app open while it downloads. ManicEMU's existing importer then adds it to the local Games library, where you can launch it.
+
+The sideload build enables access to import services through the upstream SIDE_LOAD configuration. Reopen the same Jellyfin entry to return to the saved account. The first version supports one account at a time; use Sign Out to switch servers or users.
+
+Jellyfin must expose the ROMs as indexed items. Placing arbitrary ROM files in an ordinary Jellyfin media folder does not ensure Jellyfin indexes them. If the game library is empty, check that the games are visible as items in Jellyfin itself and accessible to this account. A game-library plugin may be necessary on the server. This client does not scan server disks or add server-side indexing.
+
+## Implemented
+
+- Username/password sign-in through Jellyfin, with device-only Keychain token storage. Passwords are not persisted.
+- User-visible library selection, server-side search, and 100-item pagination.
+- Authenticated covers and filtering of known filenames to ManicEMU's game/archive formats. Items whose paths are hidden remain visible so the response filename can identify them.
+- Download to disk, cancellation, HTTP error handling, and import through `FilesImporter` with temporary-directory cleanup.
+- Server base paths and the modern `/UserViews` API with a 404 fallback to the older user-specific endpoint.
+- Authenticated requests do not follow redirects to a different origin or from HTTPS to HTTP.
+- Sign-out deletes the local credential and attempts to revoke the server session. Offline sign-out cannot guarantee remote revocation.
+
+## Scope and current limitations
+
+- This is source code, not a compiled or device-tested app. No connection to the user's server has been made.
+- Windows checks: Swift syntax parsing, Xcode source-reference checks, plist parsing, and API-contract checks. These do not establish that the app compiles.
+- All eight Swift client tests passed on the GitHub-hosted macOS runner with Xcode 26.3.
+- The hosted app build is being validated. The pinned R.swift generator trust and an Xcode type-check timeout in the upstream cheat-code decoder have been addressed. No IPA has been produced yet.
+- Games are downloaded before playing. There is no server-side game streaming, automatic launch, offline remote catalog, or Jellyfin save/progress synchronization.
+- Artwork is displayed in the remote browser; this version does not overwrite local ManicEMU artwork.
+- Multi-file games must be packaged in an archive containing all required files. A standalone CUE/M3U/GDI cannot fetch its companion files. JellyEmu-specific J3U and RomM pointer downloads are not implemented.
+- Download permission must be enabled for the Jellyfin account. Unsupported emulator systems remain unsupported.
+- Local networking is enabled through Apple's `NSAllowsLocalNetworking` setting. HTTPS is the supported choice for remote hostnames. iOS transport restrictions may reject some HTTP/IP configurations; use a valid HTTPS server address if that occurs. Certificate validation remains enabled.
+- New UI copy is English. Download UI is cancellable with a status message; it does not yet show byte-level progress or resume interrupted downloads.
+
+## Building without owning a Mac
+
+The public fork is https://github.com/Elementalzx14/ManicEMU-Jellyfin. Its **Build Jellyfin iOS IPA** workflow applies the root patch, runs the eight client tests, fetches emulator dependencies, and builds an unsigned iOS app on a GitHub-hosted Mac. Run it from the Actions tab.
+
+After a successful build, download the `ManicEMU-Jellyfin-unsigned` artifact and extract the IPA. Upload that IPA to Signulous to sign and install it. The workflow does not need Apple credentials.
+
+Failed builds retain the Xcode log for diagnosis.
+
+On a Mac, run `swift test` from the repository root to run the focused client tests. For the full app, fetch Git LFS content and recursive submodules, open the Xcode project, and build the `ManicEmuSideload` scheme. Use the upstream project requirements for its emulator dependencies.
+
+## Device acceptance checks
+
+1. Sign in with a valid account. Restart the app and reopen Jellyfin; verify the account is remembered. Try a wrong password and an unreachable server.
+2. Select a games library; compare titles and covers to Jellyfin. Search for a title containing `&` or non-ASCII characters. Verify more than 100 items can be browsed.
+3. Download a small supported single-file ROM, launch it from Games, and verify the original server file remains unchanged. Repeat the import to exercise ManicEMU's existing duplicate handling.
+4. Cancel a large download; then start another. Deny downloads for the account and verify a permission error. Test interrupted networking and server-side token revocation.
+5. Test a server installed under `/jellyfin`, a local server, and a valid HTTPS reverse proxy. Verify another user's restricted library never appears.
+6. Sign out, restart the app, and verify sign-in is required. Test iPhone and iPad presentation, search, Close, and import completion.
+
+API reference used: https://api.jellyfin.org/openapi/jellyfin-openapi-stable.json
